C=.25 J-lens-minus control difference is +0.41 raw mapped effect. `sw_pnf_02` contributes +6.15 J-lens versus +0.10 random; the other five nonzero J-lens-minus rows are -0.15, -0.05, +0.10, +0.15, +0.15. This is diagnosis evidence, not a broad-scenario gate. [tca-dose-and-measurement.md](tca-dose-and-measurement.md) shows that the C=.125 to C=.25 TCA increase is partly a changed score for byte-identical baseline text, so it is not a dose-response claim.
